    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d348-a1">

                <pb facs="0556" n="460" sameAs="frus:frus1872p1/pg460"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure.—Translation.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Lafragua to Mr. Nelson.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of Foreign Affairs</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Mexico</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-09-12"><hi rendition="#italic">September</hi> 12,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your excellency’s note and
                    annexed document of the 4th instant, concerning the American colony at Tuxpan,
                    and have the honor to state that I have transmitted copies to the treasury
                    department, in order that, after inquiry, a proper determination may be
                    taken.</p>
                <p>I take pleasure in renewing to your excellency the assurance of my high
                    consideration.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>J. M. LAFRAGUA.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
